[gregory@csri.toronto.edu (Kate M. Gregory) writes:]
[] Well, Dave, please don't take this as a flame, but as a member of the
[] "women can do everything men can do plus grow babies and then feed them"
[] school of thought, I'd be mightily offended if a gender change in hack
[] changed any of my abilities. Mightily. I like the current cosmetic-only
[] differences, like cats and dogs. 

this is clearly a sore point, i won't pursue it! but don't misunderstand
me either.  i had some idea that i could give females some unique
abilities and males some unique abilities and somehow therefore
make for (slightly different) alternative strategies.  i would not
entertain any notions that were sexist (i.e. discriminatory towards
any sex in the sense that they would be disadvantaged).  btw, a polymorph
into a new person will, in general, change your abilities but it isn't
sexist nor should it ever be.

i said a long time ago (rumor has it) that females only should be able
to lay eggs (when self-polymorphed for whatever that's worth).  i was
groping around to find a male advantage and the only one i could think
of was upper body strength (big deal with the HARD option in effect
strength is mostly inconsequential above 18!).  a dear friend (she'll
get me for that) has pointed out to me that she might be willing to
trade _initial_ strength for dexterity and retain the right to exclusive
egg-laying. seems okay by me.  males don't lay eggs although they might,
in some cases, have better luck with hatchin.  don't even mention worms
or fog clouds, etc. ...

so i was looking for real gender distinctions, nothing derogatory, that
might enhance the game.  i get the feeling that comparing gender to
cats and dogs is a big mistake and so i ask to gracefully be let off
the hook for an inadvertent blunder.  i'm not convinced that the only
way to play is to treat men and women the same (equals yes but not the
same) nor should cats be dogs (for the sake of consistent pet treatment)
but i don't have any coherent alternatives to offer up now and so i'll
let the matter rest.  no harm intended, really!

i'm removing my ring of fire resistance ...

